    "title": "Fresno lands on paranormal series after county supervisor's video - NewsBreak",
    "text": "FRESNO, Calif. ( KSEE/KGPE ) – A Fresno palm frond seemingly suspended in air has landed a spot on an international paranormal series after amassing global attention. The video was captured by Fresno County Supervisor Luis Chavez in February 2024 and shows a palm tree frond hovering over a neighborhood road about 15 feet in the air. “People have asked about the infamous canvassing video I took while knocking on doors of voters earlier this month,” he wrote on a social media post. “I sent the video to a meteorologist friend, and the best he could come up with was a ‘convergence of wind gust from opposite directions,’ whatever it was, it was a surreal experience, and I was lucky to have captured it. I’ll go with that explanation, rather than brujeria, a ghost, or another form of ghostbuster theories.” While meteorologists agree that the phenomenon can be attributed to warm air rising and lifting the front, Paranormal Caught on Camera’s first episode of season nine describes the incident as “very peculiar.” Chavez says he donated all royalties to the Central California Food Bank “to give back to our community and help ensure families have access to food and resources.” For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to CBS47 and KSEE24 | News from YourCentralValley.com.",
